WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:17.864
"Who stole my money?"

2
00:00:18.324 --> 00:00:19.405
Maggie yelled loudly.

3
00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:26.446
"Maggie," Henry warned, "you have to have proof before you start accusing people of stealing."

4
00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.707
He looked into the cashbox that Maggie was holding.

5
00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:31.848
It was completely empty.

6
00:00:32.528 --> 00:00:36.850
"Are you sure you didn't take the money out and put it in your pocket or something?"

7
00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:37.971
he asked her.

8
00:00:37.991 --> 00:00:40.272
"Yeah," Cole said.

9
00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:42.073
"You probably put the money somewhere."

10
00:00:42.093 --> 00:00:43.914
"No way!"

11
00:00:44.414 --> 00:00:46.015
Maggie looked really upset now.

12
00:00:46.035 --> 00:00:49.757
"There was a lot of cash in here five minutes ago when Mrs.

13
00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:52.439
Martin paid for little Marty's lemonade."

14
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.142
She pointed to the woman standing nearby, who was still talking on her cell phone.

15
00:00:58.902 --> 00:01:02.064
The little boy, Marty Martin, had dropped his mother's hand.

16
00:01:02.668 --> 00:01:06.571
He was staring at Maggie and banging a toy suitcase against his knees.

17
00:01:06.591 --> 00:01:09.453
"Okay," Henry said.

18
00:01:09.473 --> 00:01:13.756
"Then maybe the money blew away when you opened the box."

19
00:01:14.516 --> 00:01:17.779
"It's not even windy today," Maggie said.

20
00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:19.400
She shook her head.

21
00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:23.342
"I think someone stole my horseback-riding money.

22
00:01:25.104 --> 00:01:26.725
And I want to know who it was!"

23
00:01:27.726 --> 00:01:29.607
By now everyone except Mrs.

24
00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:30.988
Martin was staring at her.

25
00:01:31.628 --> 00:01:34.669
The two teenage girls giggled and whispered to each other.

26
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.230
Maggie looked at them.

27
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.791
"Was it you two?"

28
00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:38.871
she asked.

29
00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:40.532
"Did you take my money?"

30
00:01:40.552 --> 00:01:43.193
"No," one of the girls said.

31
00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:45.014
"We're not crooks.

32
00:01:45.794 --> 00:01:47.955
Come on, Jill, let's get out of here."

33
00:01:47.975 --> 00:01:50.096
"Yeah." Her friend giggled.

34
00:01:50.116 --> 00:01:52.777
"Before she accuses us of something else!"

35
00:01:53.437 --> 00:01:55.478
The two of them laughed and walked off.

36
00:01:56.419 --> 00:01:59.300
Maggie glared at them, and then looked around again.

37
00:02:00.544 --> 00:02:02.085
"Maybe it was Ryan!"

38
00:02:02.665 --> 00:02:03.146
she said.

39
00:02:03.726 --> 00:02:05.647
Ryan had finished chugging his lemonade.

40
00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:09.089
Now he was jumping his skateboard on and off the curb.

41
00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:11.971
"Did you steal my money when I wasn't looking?"

42
00:02:12.391 --> 00:02:13.191
Maggie asked.

43
00:02:13.972 --> 00:02:15.473
He stopped and stared at Maggie.

44
00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:18.434
"Dude, I didn't take your money.

45
00:02:19.195 --> 00:02:21.836
Maybe you should have watched it better," he said.

46
00:02:22.777 --> 00:02:24.578
Then he skated off down the street.

47
00:02:24.598 --> 00:02:26.859
"Hey! Get back here!"

48
00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:28.000
Maggie yelled.

49
00:02:28.568 --> 00:02:31.429
But Ryan ignored her, skidding around the corner.

50
00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:36.031
Nathan and his little sister Nora were listening to everything.

51
00:02:36.051 --> 00:02:40.913
"It wasn't me," Nathan said before Maggie could say anything to him.

52
00:02:40.933 --> 00:02:42.554
"I promise."

53
00:02:42.574 --> 00:02:44.394
"Are you sure?"

54
00:02:44.795 --> 00:02:45.415
Maggie said.

55
00:02:45.435 --> 00:02:47.396
"It had to be someone!"

56
00:02:48.156 --> 00:02:49.456
Nora poked her brother.

57
00:02:49.476 --> 00:02:53.698
"I think I hear Mommy calling us," she said.

58
00:02:53.718 --> 00:02:56.719
"I didn't hear anything," Henry said.

59
00:02:56.739 --> 00:02:57.960
"Me neither.

60
00:02:58.592 --> 00:03:00.993
But I'd better go check," Nathan said.

61
00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:03.674
"Come on, Nora, let's go home."

62
00:03:03.694 --> 00:03:06.595
"No!" Nora said.

63
00:03:07.216 --> 00:03:08.396
She loved to argue.

64
00:03:08.416 --> 00:03:10.137
"I don't want to!"

65
00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:13.518
Nathan was used to her, so he just ignored her.

66
00:03:14.039 --> 00:03:17.360
But when he rushed off toward their house, she hurried after him.

67
00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.122
Maggie was looking around for more possible thieves.

68
00:03:21.902 --> 00:03:22.582
"Where did Mrs.

69
00:03:22.662 --> 00:03:23.923
Martin and Marty go?"

70
00:03:24.443 --> 00:03:25.003
she asked.

71
00:03:25.023 --> 00:03:26.684
"They left."

72
00:03:27.116 --> 00:03:28.316
Cole pointed down the block.

73
00:03:28.897 --> 00:03:30.497
Henry looked and saw Mrs.

74
00:03:30.557 --> 00:03:31.797
Martin wandering away.

75
00:03:32.598 --> 00:03:34.618
Her cell phone was still pressed to her ear.

76
00:03:35.498 --> 00:03:37.859
Little Marty was skipping along after her.

77
00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:41.300
"I don't think you need to accuse Mrs.

78
00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.781
Martin of being the thief," Henry said.

79
00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.741
"She's a police detective, remember?"

80
00:03:48.042 --> 00:03:48.722
Cole nodded.

81
00:03:48.742 --> 00:03:52.663
"She catches thieves—she's not one herself," he said.

82
00:03:52.683 --> 00:03:54.484
"Maybe you're right."

83
00:03:54.844 --> 00:03:55.604
Maggie frowned.

84
00:03:56.248 --> 00:03:59.749
"But someone stole my money, and I want to know who it was."

85
00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:03.450
"Calm down," Henry told his cousin.

86
00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:07.051
"You're not going to figure it out by yelling at everyone."

87
00:04:07.071 --> 00:04:10.012
"How else am I going to get an answer?"

88
00:04:10.612 --> 00:04:11.392
Maggie asked.

89
00:04:12.272 --> 00:04:15.253
"Think about it logically," Henry said.

90
00:04:15.273 --> 00:04:22.275
"Whoever took that money is a thief, which means he or she is probably a liar too."

91
00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.936
"Good point," Cole said with a nod.

92
00:04:25.484 --> 00:04:27.405
"Guess you'd better say good-bye to that money, Maggie."

93
00:04:28.286 --> 00:04:29.607
Maggie scowled at him.

94
00:04:29.627 --> 00:04:31.148
"Be quiet, Cole!"

95
00:04:32.108 --> 00:04:35.110
"She doesn't need to give up," Henry told his friend.

96
00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.593
"We just need to think like detectives.

97
00:04:39.613 --> 00:04:43.776
I bet if the three of us work together, we can figure out who took the money."

98
00:04:43.796 --> 00:04:47.038
"We're just kids," Maggie said.

99
00:04:47.058 --> 00:04:50.401
"How are we supposed to think like detectives?"

100
00:04:51.221 --> 00:04:51.761
"I know!"

101
00:04:52.242 --> 00:04:52.822
Cole said.

102
00:04:52.842 --> 00:04:55.364
"I watched a mystery movie on TV last week.

103
00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.182
The detective started by figuring out who the suspects were."

104
00:04:59.202 --> 00:05:03.145
"We already know that," Maggie interrupted.

105
00:05:03.165 --> 00:05:07.407
"It had to be someone who was nearby when the money disappeared."

106
00:05:07.908 --> 00:05:08.828
Henry smiled.

107
00:05:08.848 --> 00:05:13.952
"See? We're already thinking like detectives," he said.

108
00:05:13.972 --> 00:05:19.596
"Okay, so we know approximately when the money disappeared.

109
00:05:20.256 --> 00:05:22.077
Who was nearby during that time?"

110
00:05:22.097 --> 00:05:25.960
"You just saw them," Maggie said.

111
00:05:26.664 --> 00:05:29.307
"Nathan and Nora, Mrs.

112
00:05:29.407 --> 00:05:33.570
Martin and Marty, Ryan, and those two teenage girls.

113
00:05:34.351 --> 00:05:35.872
Oh, and you two of course."

114
00:05:36.553 --> 00:05:38.754
"Nobody else stopped by before Henry and I got here?"

115
00:05:39.115 --> 00:05:39.895
Cole asked.

116
00:05:39.915 --> 00:05:43.458
"Like a stranger or a suspicious-looking deliveryman?"

117
00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:45.940
Maggie shook her head.

118
00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.542
"Nope. Just the people you saw."

119
00:05:49.223 --> 00:05:50.244
Cole bit his lip.

120
00:05:50.264 --> 00:05:52.826
"That means the thief had to be someone we know."

121
00:05:53.507 --> 00:05:54.848
They all looked at each other.

122
00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.765
"It's someone from our very own neighborhood!"

123
00:05:59.326 --> 00:05:59.967
said Henry.
